\title{Symbols with one second-order coefficient}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{The circle mesh couples nearest neighbors. A symmetric
difference of longer but still finite range has several
coefficients, and its symbol need not be a multiple of
#{1-\cos\theta}. Which of those coefficients remain visible
in a fixed Fourier moment, and in the means of equal blocks,
once the number of vertices grows?}
